From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sky Malice <skym@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:04:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [upstream] [Gradle] Include canonical compile_resources
 srcjar in generate_gradle

In crrev.com/c/8253833, bundled srcjar extraction was added to
generate_gradle.py, but _IsUsefulSrcJar unconditionally excluded all
__compile_resources.srcjars. Consequently, R classes (such as
org.chromium.chrome.browser.omnibox.R) were never extracted or
indexed in Android Studio projects.

This updates generate_gradle.py to dynamically select and extract the
canonical __compile_resources.srcjar based on the targets and mode:
- In --all mode, picks the preferred root browser target (such as
  chrome_apk or chrome_public_apk) to avoid duplicate class collisions
  across APK targets in the single combined module.
- In targeted or split-project mode, allows each root target to include
  its own __compile_resources.srcjar.

